# Tenant plans gate features. The entitlement is a disjunction of
# CLOSED maps, one per plan (the tls-style conditional-shape idiom):
# unifying a concrete `plan` kills every other branch, and the
# surviving closed map pins what that plan may enable --
# "if plan=free then sso=false" is a shape, not a rule.
#
# NOTE: candidates must carry entitlement.plan themselves. The schema
# also ties entitlement.plan to tenant.plan by reference (tenant.aon),
# but under `vet` that cross-reference is resolved against the schema
# alone and never re-checked against the merged data -- a branch
# keyed only on the reference silently passes (see README,
# "Stale references under vet").
Entitlement: type(
  close({ plan:"free" sso:false scim:false auditLog:false })
  | close({ plan:"pro" sso:boolean scim:false auditLog:boolean })
  | close({ plan:"enterprise" sso:boolean scim:boolean auditLog:true })
)
